E. THE GENUINELY NEW SLOT k=7 -- speculative closed form, first testable at j=8
==============================================================================
    j=8 is the first order with k=7 < j, so c_4 was never observed before.
    Three separate extrapolations from m<=3 were registered. Scoring them:

    (i) NUMERATORS  a_m^A = 3+44*16^(m-1),  a_m^E = 4+33*9^(m-1),  a_m^C = 23
        A  predicted   180227   observed   180227   CONFIRMED
        E  predicted    24061   observed    24061   CONFIRMED
        C  predicted       23   observed       23   CONFIRMED

    (ii) SLICE RATIOS  d_m^A/d_m^C = 4^(2m-1),  d_m^E/d_m^C = 3^(2m-1)
        A  predicted 4^7 =    16384   observed 16384   CONFIRMED
        E  predicted 3^7 =     2187   observed 2187   CONFIRMED

    (iii) BASE SEQUENCE  d_m^C = (3m)!/(2m-2)!  ->  predicted d_4^C = 665280
        observed d_4^C = 604800   ratio predicted/observed = 11/10
        *** REFUTED *** -- this was the one guess that failed.

    Resulting measured constants:
        c_4^A = 180227/9909043200
        c_4^E = 24061/1322697600
        c_4^C = 23/604800

  VERDICT E: numerator laws and slice ratios CONFIRMED at held-out
             m=4 (True); the factorial base guess is refuted.  The independent
             referee identifies the measured C constants by Bernoulli/Faulhaber.

